  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 7.15,
      "end": 23.43,
      "text": "On 275 and 285, and in stereo on VHF, this is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.43,
      "end": 30.3,
      "text": "Well, hello there. Thomas the Vance here. Welcome, once again, to the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.3,
      "end": 34.3,
      "text": "And tonight we continue to air the live sets of the Friday Rock Show recorded at Reading.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.3,
      "end": 42.3,
      "text": "I've not heard the results of the recording session yet, but Tony Wilson, producer, and Bill Aitken, who mixed it, reckon this one tonight is a gasp.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.3,
      "end": 56.55,
      "text": "It's Steve Hackett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.55,
      "end": 59.13,
      "text": "We've got classic cuts by Cream, The Tangs and The Birds,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.23,
      "end": 61.77,
      "text": "and new releases by Skyhooks, Bob Dylan and City Boy,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.85,
      "end": 62.81,
      "text": "also Molly Hatchet.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.88,
      "end": 66.24,
      "text": "And this week, there won't be a new Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.24,
      "end": 67.92,
      "text": "because we didn't get one right answer,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.04,
      "end": 70.2,
      "text": "but we have edited highlights of last week's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.2,
      "end": 71.4,
      "text": "to give you a second chance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.39,
      "end": 75.15,
      "text": "Tonight, we start with the James Gang.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.15,
      "end": 81.55,
      "text": "Anybody else but ACDC, and ACDC it certainly was,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 604.57,
      "end": 605.81,
      "text": "from their album Highway to Hell,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 605.89,
      "end": 607.17,
      "text": "which is out on Atlantic at the moment,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 607.25,
      "end": 609.01,
      "text": "are doing remarkably well, thank you very much.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 609.01,
      "end": 610.71,
      "text": "The track was called The Girls Got Rhythm,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 611.13,
      "end": 613.29,
      "text": "and before that, something from a really good old album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 613.29,
      "end": 617.77,
      "text": "called bang featured the music of the james gang and the track was standing in the rain",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 619.24,
      "end": 626.38,
      "text": "also featured of course the guitar playing of the late tommy boland who is sadly missed played that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 626.38,
      "end": 631.18,
      "text": "specially for a gentleman by the name of chris blanchard who lives in sunnybank in penn epelum",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 631.18,
      "end": 643.2,
      "text": "hollywell in Clwyd who says more tommy boland unfortunately only out of our library which",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 643.2,
      "end": 646.48,
      "text": "is a darn shame here's a track from a new album though you've heard the track before",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1242.27,
      "end": 1243.41,
      "text": "And that's an Australian band",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1243.41,
      "end": 1245.29,
      "text": "by the name of Skyhooks, who recorded an album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1245.29,
      "end": 1247.33,
      "text": "in Melbourne and also in Sydney.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1247.51,
      "end": 1249.43,
      "text": "The album's called Guilty Until Proven",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1249.43,
      "end": 1251.29,
      "text": "Insane. It's out on United",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1251.29,
      "end": 1253.13,
      "text": "Artists, and the track was Women in Uniform.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1253.63,
      "end": 1255.25,
      "text": "I think I should dedicate that to the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1255.25,
      "end": 1257.03,
      "text": "Peeler, the schoolgirl's friend.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1258.04,
      "end": 1259.44,
      "text": "Prior to that, you heard a couple of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1259.44,
      "end": 1261.32,
      "text": "tracks from a new album. Well, at least it's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1261.32,
      "end": 1263.4,
      "text": "going to be new, as far as you're concerned, in about a couple",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1263.4,
      "end": 1264.56,
      "text": "of weeks' time, when it's released.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1265.2,
      "end": 1267.68,
      "text": "It's called Unleashed in the East,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1267.82,
      "end": 1269.48,
      "text": "live in Japan, and it featured",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1269.48,
      "end": 1271.48,
      "text": "Judas Priest. You heard the Green Man and the She,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1271.48,
      "end": 1273.6,
      "text": "which was out on a 12-incher some time ago,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1273.88,
      "end": 1275.16,
      "text": "and also a track called The Ripper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1282.44,
      "end": 1285.22,
      "text": "10.21 on the Friday Rock Show, here's Mr. D.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1285.78,
      "end": 1287.1,
      "text": "Change my way of thinking",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1287.1,
      "end": 1291.9,
      "text": "Real classic, Cream, from way back in 1967.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1865.9,
      "end": 1867.52,
      "text": "We played it off the LP Heavy Cream.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1867.68,
      "end": 1868.94,
      "text": "It was the sunshine of your love,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1869.02,
      "end": 1871.06,
      "text": "and before that, something from the new Dylan album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1871.26,
      "end": 1872.36,
      "text": "Slow Train Coming.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1872.56,
      "end": 1875.22,
      "text": "The track was Gonna Change My Way of Thinking.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1878.2,
      "end": 1880.0,
      "text": "Played both those tracks for one gentleman,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1880.54,
      "end": 1881.92,
      "text": "because he's in hospital at the moment.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1882.64,
      "end": 1884.06,
      "text": "He's in the Milford Chest Hospital",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1884.06,
      "end": 1885.48,
      "text": "in Godalming in Surrey",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1885.48,
      "end": 1888.14,
      "text": "and he describes himself as the kid",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1888.14,
      "end": 1890.22,
      "text": "aged 25, a gentleman by the name of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1890.22,
      "end": 1891.44,
      "text": "Tommy Barker, Tommy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1891.44,
      "end": 1893.78,
      "text": "and indeed everybody is in hospital",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1893.78,
      "end": 1895.96,
      "text": "hope you get better soon, but it's not",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1895.96,
      "end": 1897.94,
      "text": "too uncomfortable, I'm one of the lucky ones",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1897.94,
      "end": 1900.18,
      "text": "I've never been in, Tom",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1900.18,
      "end": 1902.22,
      "text": "nice car, I hope you enjoy the music",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1902.22,
      "end": 1918.25,
      "text": "if you've got them to hand, I think now",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1918.25,
      "end": 1920.19,
      "text": "is the time to put on the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1920.19,
      "end": 1922.1,
      "text": "headset and listen to this",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1922.1,
      "end": 1923.96,
      "text": "duologue in stereo",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1923.96,
      "end": 1929.96,
      "text": "we played that just a few weeks ago and so",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2679.91,
      "end": 2681.89,
      "text": "many people wrote in and asked us to tell them",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2681.89,
      "end": 2688.26,
      "text": "exactly what it was it's from the album force majeure that came out on virgin some time ago",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2688.26,
      "end": 2698.06,
      "text": "it's tangerine dream and cloud burst played especially for mark cheshire of rodborne rail",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2698.06,
      "end": 2704.36,
      "text": "farm i think it is the farm that has rails on it malmsbury in wiltshire and also for a load of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2704.36,
      "end": 2709.22,
      "text": "people on behalf of simon morley of number 102 avondale road it's which in suffolk he wants me",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2709.22,
      "end": 2713.48,
      "text": "to mention loads of people including benny and brian and so that's i think brian is called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2713.48,
      "end": 2714.48,
      "text": "Sandra, or vice versa.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2714.9,
      "end": 2717.12,
      "text": "Biggles, who sometimes is called Georgina.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2717.6,
      "end": 2719.24,
      "text": "Barry and Wendy and Sarah and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2719.24,
      "end": 2720.78,
      "text": "Mitchel Eschke.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2721.16,
      "end": 2723.88,
      "text": "And Kathy and Yogi and Moe and Kenton and Andrew and Eggie.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2724.22,
      "end": 2725.74,
      "text": "And Thunder Thighs Jackson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2726.4,
      "end": 2728.72,
      "text": "And all the rest of the rock freaks at Northgate High.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2729.38,
      "end": 2731.28,
      "text": "Special mention to a lady by the name of Sarah.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2731.84,
      "end": 2733.26,
      "text": "And prior to that, we heard Gary Newman",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2733.26,
      "end": 2734.88,
      "text": "in the track from the album in the charts",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2734.88,
      "end": 2736.14,
      "text": "called The Pleasure Principle.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2736.54,
      "end": 2738.04,
      "text": "The track was M.E.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2738.7,
      "end": 2744.3,
      "text": "It's a quarter to eleven.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2744.76,
      "end": 2747.76,
      "text": "Great band, City Boy,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3272.96,
      "end": 3274.2,
      "text": "and the title track from their new album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3274.2,
      "end": 3275.18,
      "text": "which is out on Vertigo.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3275.28,
      "end": 3277.54,
      "text": "The album's called The Day the Earth Caught Fire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3277.68,
      "end": 3280.63,
      "text": "Before that, a real classic from times gone by,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3280.79,
      "end": 3283.25,
      "text": "The Birds, from the album Fifth Dimension.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3283.35,
      "end": 3284.39,
      "text": "Eight Miles High was the track,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3284.79,
      "end": 3289.05,
      "text": "and it was from Anthony Leake of [redacted address],",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3289.49,
      "end": 3291.45,
      "text": "Grange Park, Chard in Somerset.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3291.97,
      "end": 3294.45,
      "text": "For Martin, and for Lou, and for Pete,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3294.73,
      "end": 3296.41,
      "text": "and for everybody down there in Plymouth.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3296.67,
      "end": 3299.45,
      "text": "Traffic news from Radio 1!",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3300.37,
      "end": 3302.15,
      "text": "News has just come in from our motoring unit",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3302.15,
      "end": 3304.13,
      "text": "of serious delays on the M1 approaching",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3304.13,
      "end": 3306.31,
      "text": "Junction 15 near Northampton.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3306.55,
      "end": 3308.31,
      "text": "Road work has caused two-way traffic",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3308.31,
      "end": 3310.31,
      "text": "on one carriageway, and there have",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3310.31,
      "end": 3312.23,
      "text": "been some accidents, so the traffic is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3312.23,
      "end": 3314.31,
      "text": "now tailing back for about nine",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3314.31,
      "end": 3316.29,
      "text": "miles to Junction 14 near",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3316.29,
      "end": 3318.27,
      "text": "Newport Pagnol. Drivers going north",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3318.27,
      "end": 3320.31,
      "text": "on the M1 are advised to use other",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3320.31,
      "end": 3322.05,
      "text": "routes between Junctions",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3322.05,
      "end": 3324.37,
      "text": "14 and 15, as it may be sometime",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3324.37,
      "end": 3326.19,
      "text": "before this long queue of vehicles is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3326.19,
      "end": 3328.25,
      "text": "cleared between Newport, Pagnol",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3328.25,
      "end": 3328.95,
      "text": "and Northampton.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3328.95,
      "end": 3349.26,
      "text": "wherever you're driving do take care 5 to 11 and time for the friday night connection well we",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3349.26,
      "end": 3354.9,
      "text": "started this program last november and it's the first time it's ever happened not one right answer",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3354.9,
      "end": 3363.38,
      "text": "you got the tracks right no problem but as i said last week don't go for the obvious answer but you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3363.38,
      "end": 3372.1,
      "text": "all did the answer did not lie in pharmaceuticals or drugs or chemicals it lies somewhere else it's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3372.1,
      "end": 3376.72,
      "text": "Definitely in there in the three tracks, but it wasn't pharmaceuticals, drugs, or chemicals.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3377.04,
      "end": 3378.14,
      "text": "Now, what is it?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3379.81,
      "end": 3381.61,
      "text": "I'll tell you what, we'll give you another chance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3381.99,
      "end": 3384.37,
      "text": "Generous to a fault we are here on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3384.89,
      "end": 3386.41,
      "text": "And I'm going to give you a clue.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3387.45,
      "end": 3393.83,
      "text": "The clue is, and it's been put together, and I add by a gentleman from the part of the world that's going to become obvious by this word,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3394.27,
      "end": 3396.05,
      "text": "the clue is guitar-ton.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3397.16,
      "end": 3401.18,
      "text": "And now, a sort of, well, mixture of the tracks.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3401.18,
      "end": 3412.58,
      "text": "the noted producer of this program is on holiday over there in cyprus at the moment i'll give away",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3632.2,
      "end": 3637.75,
      "text": "20 pounds in terms of a record token for the right answer this week i can only do that because",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3637.75,
      "end": 3644.77,
      "text": "he's not here because he's so tight when he walks he squeaks in fact i can hear him from here so",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3644.77,
      "end": 3651.28,
      "text": "it's 20 quids worth record tokens if you can tell me what the connection is once again in the friday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3651.28,
      "end": 3654.8,
      "text": "night connection that we played last week you know the tracks everybody got the tracks right but",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3654.8,
      "end": 3656.14,
      "text": "Nobody got the right connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3656.42,
      "end": 3659.26,
      "text": "Not pharmaceuticals, not drugs, not chemicals.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3661.12,
      "end": 3667.04,
      "text": "Answers, postcard, letter, any communication form you like to Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3667.7,
      "end": 3673.84,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3675.03,
      "end": 3678.34,
      "text": "That ought to, uh, where? Swing your kilt?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3678.86,
      "end": 3689.06,
      "text": "And from the southern part of the United States of America, by the name of Molly Hatchett,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4229.03,
      "end": 4230.39,
      "text": "from Molly Hatchett Live.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4230.39,
      "end": 4233.43,
      "text": "And if you get the special promotional issue of the album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4233.53,
      "end": 4235.61,
      "text": "you'll get two albums for your money, which is nice.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4236.07,
      "end": 4239.55,
      "text": "It's out on Epic, and the track you heard there was called Dreams I'll Never See.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4240.01,
      "end": 4244.47,
      "text": "Now, they are going to be on the programme next week on our, if you like, in-concert spot.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4244.91,
      "end": 4248.39,
      "text": "Before that, you heard something by Tycoon, a track from their album out on Arista.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4248.81,
      "end": 4250.31,
      "text": "The track was Too Late, New York City.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4250.67,
      "end": 4254.63,
      "text": "And in the coming weeks, on the Friday Rock Show, you can also hear The Police.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4255.07,
      "end": 4262.87,
      "text": "It's got to be a top five single. It really has to be.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4423.71,
      "end": 4425.77,
      "text": "Written by Sting, that's the new single by The Police,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4425.77,
      "end": 4427.15,
      "text": "and it's called Message in a Bottle.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4427.35,
      "end": 4429.41,
      "text": "We won't, unfortunately, be able to bring you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4429.41,
      "end": 4431.17,
      "text": "the set that they did in Reading,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4431.77,
      "end": 4433.53,
      "text": "but we will feature very heavily",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4433.53,
      "end": 4435.19,
      "text": "their new album when it comes out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4435.19,
      "end": 4436.65,
      "text": "in about a fortnight's time.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4436.87,
      "end": 4438.49,
      "text": "But now we can reminisce about Reading",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4438.49,
      "end": 4440.55,
      "text": "and for the next 45 minutes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4440.75,
      "end": 4443.37,
      "text": "this is Ace Music from Steve Hackett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4443.93,
      "end": 4446.93,
      "text": "Steve Frank today, the Octagon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5622.6,
      "end": 5625.6,
      "text": "Steve Hackett has recorded live",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7252.54,
      "end": 7253.66,
      "text": "at the Reading Festival.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7253.94,
      "end": 7254.8,
      "text": "The tracks that you heard were",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7254.8,
      "end": 7257.12,
      "text": "I Know What I Like, Clocks, Spectral Mornings,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7257.12,
      "end": 7258.98,
      "text": "Tower Struck Down, Octagon,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7258.98,
      "end": 7261.54,
      "text": "Everyday Tiger Moth and Please Don't Touch",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7261.54,
      "end": 7263.04,
      "text": "and the band were made up of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7263.04,
      "end": 7265.08,
      "text": "Pete Hicks, vocals, tambourine and bass pedals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7265.08,
      "end": 7267.1,
      "text": "John Shearer on the drums, percussion",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7267.1,
      "end": 7268.46,
      "text": "and primeval screams",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7268.46,
      "end": 7270.4,
      "text": "Dick Cadbury, bass and vocals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7270.4,
      "end": 7272.84,
      "text": "John Hackett, flute, guitar, bass pedals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7272.84,
      "end": 7274.88,
      "text": "Nick Magnus on keyboards",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7274.88,
      "end": 7276.12,
      "text": "and Steve Hackett himself",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7276.12,
      "end": 7279.36,
      "text": "on guitar, guitar synthesizer and occasional vocals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7279.36,
      "end": 7282.39,
      "text": "our engineer for the session",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7282.39,
      "end": 7283.41,
      "text": "there was Mike Robinson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7283.41,
      "end": 7284.75,
      "text": "it was mixed by Bill Aitken",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7284.75,
      "end": 7286.41,
      "text": "and it was produced by Tony Wilson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7286.41,
      "end": 7289.61,
      "text": "and it sounded pretty good in the studio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7289.61,
      "end": 7293.15,
      "text": "I would think equally as amazing at home.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7294.36,
      "end": 7295.6,
      "text": "Don't forget Mike Reed and the Peeler,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7295.74,
      "end": 7296.98,
      "text": "Monday to Thursday on Radio 1,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7297.06,
      "end": 7297.78,
      "text": "on Rock On Tomorrow,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7297.96,
      "end": 7299.14,
      "text": "interviews with Jimmy Percy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7299.14,
      "end": 7301.62,
      "text": "on why he's rejoined Sham 69.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7302.3,
      "end": 7304.22,
      "text": "Loudon Wainwright will be having a chat with us,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7304.6,
      "end": 7306.3,
      "text": "and Richard Skinner is presenting a feature",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7306.3,
      "end": 7307.54,
      "text": "on the Star Revival.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7308.02,
      "end": 7309.76,
      "text": "Our engineer tonight on the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7309.76,
      "end": 7310.32,
      "text": "has been John.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7310.76,
      "end": 7311.28,
      "text": "Thank you, John.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7314.02,
      "end": 7315.5,
      "text": "Don't forget, Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7315.54,
      "end": 7316.96,
      "text": "with all those clues you should be getting it,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7317.02,
      "end": 7318.24,
      "text": "£20 record token offered.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7318.7,
      "end": 7320.16,
      "text": "Wherever you are, take care of yourselves.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7320.72,
      "end": 7323.06,
      "text": "I'll see you tomorrow for Rock on at 4 o'clock on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7323.3,
      "end": 7325.94,
      "text": "From me, Thomas Vance in London, God bless and good night.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}